.SS "virtual bool Assimp::BaseImporter::CanRead (const std::string & pFile, \fBIOSystem\fP * pIOHandler, bool checkSig) const\fR [pure virtual]\fP"
Returns whether the class can handle the format of the given file\&.
.PP
The implementation is expected to perform a full check of the file structure, possibly searching the first bytes of the file for magic identifiers or keywords\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpFile\fP Path and file name of the file to be examined\&. 
.br
\fIpIOHandler\fP The IO handler to use for accessing any file\&. 
.br
\fIcheckSig\fP Legacy; do not use\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the class can read this file, false if not or if unsure\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "static bool Assimp::BaseImporter::CheckMagicToken (\fBIOSystem\fP * pIOHandler, const std::string & pFile, const \fBvoid\fP * magic, std::size_t num, unsigned int offset = \fR0\fP, unsigned int size = \fR4\fP)\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Check whether a file starts with one or more magic tokens\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpFile\fP Input file 
.br
\fIpIOHandler\fP IO system to be used 
.br
\fImagic\fP n magic tokens @params num Size of magic 
.br
\fIoffset\fP Offset from file start where tokens are located 
.br
\fISize\fP of one token, in bytes\&. Maximally 16 bytes\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if one of the given tokens was found
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
For convenience, the check is also performed for the byte-swapped variant of all tokens (big endian)\&. Only for tokens of size 2,4\&. 
.RE
.PP

