.SS "virtual \fBvoid\fP Assimp::BaseImporter::InternReadFile (const std::string & pFile, \fBaiScene\fP * pScene, \fBIOSystem\fP * pIOHandler)\fR [protected]\fP, \fR [pure virtual]\fP"
Imports the given file into the given scene structure\&. The function is expected to throw an ImportErrorException if there is an error\&. If it terminates normally, the data in \fBaiScene\fP is expected to be correct\&. Override this function to implement the actual importing\&. 
.br
 The output scene must meet the following requirements:
.br
 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
At least a root node must be there, even if its only purpose is to reference one mesh\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBaiMesh::mPrimitiveTypes\fP may be 0\&. The types of primitives in the mesh are determined automatically in this case\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
the vertex data is stored in a pseudo-indexed 'verbose' format\&. In fact this means that every vertex that is referenced by a face is unique\&. Or the other way round: a vertex index may not occur twice in a single \fBaiMesh\fP\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBaiAnimation::mDuration\fP may be -1\&. \fBAssimp\fP determines the length of the animation automatically in this case as the length of the longest animation channel\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBaiMesh::mBitangents\fP may be nullptr if tangents and normals are given\&. In this case bitangents are computed as the cross product between normal and tangent\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
There needn't be a material\&. If none is there a default material is generated\&. However, it is recommended practice for loaders to generate a default material for yourself that matches the default material setting for the file format better than \fBAssimp\fP's generic default material\&. Note that default materials \fIshould\fP be named AI_DEFAULT_MATERIAL_NAME if they're just color-shaded or AI_DEFAULT_TEXTURED_MATERIAL_NAME if they define a (dummy) texture\&.  
.PP
If the AI_SCENE_FLAGS_INCOMPLETE-Flag is \fBnot\fP set:
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
at least one mesh must be there 
.IP "\(bu" 2
there may be no meshes with 0 vertices or faces 
.PP
This won't be checked (except by the validation step): \fBAssimp\fP will crash if one of the conditions is not met!
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpFile\fP Path of the file to be imported\&. 
.br
\fIpScene\fP The scene object to hold the imported data\&. nullptr is not a valid parameter\&. 
.br
\fIpIOHandler\fP The IO handler to use for any file access\&. nullptr is not a valid parameter\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBaiScene\fP * Assimp::BaseImporter::ReadFile (\fBImporter\fP * pImp, const std::string & pFile, \fBIOSystem\fP * pIOHandler)"
Imports the given file and returns the imported data\&. If the import succeeds, ownership of the data is transferred to the caller\&. If the import fails, nullptr is returned\&. The function takes care that any partially constructed data is destroyed beforehand\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpImp\fP \fBImporter\fP object hosting this loader\&. 
.br
\fIpFile\fP Path of the file to be imported\&. 
.br
\fIpIOHandler\fP IO-Handler used to open this and possible other files\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The imported data or nullptr if failed\&. If it failed a human-readable error description can be retrieved by calling \fBGetErrorText()\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This function is not intended to be overridden\&. Implement \fBInternReadFile()\fP to do the import\&. If an exception is thrown somewhere in \fBInternReadFile()\fP, this function will catch it and transform it into a suitable response to the caller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "static bool Assimp::BaseImporter::SearchFileHeaderForToken (\fBIOSystem\fP * pIOSystem, const std::string & file, const char ** tokens, std::size_t numTokens, unsigned int searchBytes = \fR200\fP, bool tokensSol = \fRfalse\fP, bool noAlphaBeforeTokens = \fRfalse\fP)\fR [static]\fP"
A utility for \fBCanRead()\fP\&.
.PP
The function searches the header of a file for a specific token and returns true if this token is found\&. This works for text files only\&. There is a rudimentary handling of UNICODE files\&. The comparison is case independent\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpIOSystem\fP IO System to work with 
.br
\fIfile\fP File name of the file 
.br
\fItokens\fP List of tokens to search for 
.br
\fInumTokens\fP Size of the token array 
.br
\fIsearchBytes\fP Number of bytes to be searched for the tokens\&. 
.RE
.PP

